# ── Default-deny (allowlist) build context ───────────────────────────────────
# The build context is the repo ROOT (docker-compose `context: .`). Two images
# build from here:
#   management-api    docker/management-api/Dockerfile
#   pqc-ca-custodian  docker/pqc-ca-custodian/Dockerfile
#
# RATIONALE, this is a PKI/CA product, so the context is treated default-DENY.
# A blocklist-style .dockerignore is unsafe here: any new secret path (a stray
# *.key, a new secrets/ file, .env, admin-cert/, certs/, pki/) is otherwise
# uploaded into the build context and baked into the registry build cache by
# default, until someone remembers to add it. Instead we ignore EVERYTHING (`*`),
# re-include ONLY the paths the two root-context builds actually COPY, then
# RE-EXCLUDE secret material even under those re-included roots. dockerignore
# evaluates patterns in order and the LAST match wins, so the re-excludes are
# placed AFTER the re-includes to guarantee they win.
#
# What the builds actually need (verified against both Dockerfiles' COPY lines):
#   management-api    pqc-mtls-management-api/ source, package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml,
#                     pnpm-workspace.yaml, tsconfig*, nest-cli.json, src/. It runs
#                     `pnpm install` + `pnpm build` INSIDE the image, so the host's
#                     node_modules/ and dist/ are NOT needed and MUST be excluded:
#                     pnpm lays out node_modules with symlinks that buildkit cannot
#                     COPY-merge over the image's freshly installed ones. Plus
#                     docker/base/openssl-compiled.tar.gz.
#   pqc-ca-custodian  docker/base/openssl-compiled.tar.gz and
#                     docker/pqc-ca-custodian/custodian.js.
# NOTE: docker/base/openssl-compiled.tar.gz is gitignored/untracked but IS a
# required build input, so none of the re-excludes below may match it.

# 1) Ignore everything by default.
*

# 2) Re-include ONLY the two roots the builds COPY from. Re-including a directory
#    pulls in its whole subtree; step 3 carves the secrets back out.
!docker
!pqc-mtls-management-api

# 3) RE-EXCLUDE secret / non-build material. Most of these are top-level and thus
#    already denied by `*`; they are listed explicitly as defense-in-depth and
#    documentation, so that no future `!`-re-include can accidentally leak them.
secrets/
admin-cert/
certs/
.env
**/.env
pki/out/
pki/
**/*.key
**/*.pem

# Host dev-machine artifacts living inside the re-included submodule. These are
# rebuilt inside the image; the host copies must never overwrite them (see the
# node_modules symlink note above).
pqc-mtls-management-api/.git
pqc-mtls-management-api/node_modules
pqc-mtls-management-api/dist

# Bulky, non-build junk that would only bloat the context and the build cache.
*.pptx
*.pdf
**/.DS_Store
